1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,312
The Story of Chocolate.

2
00:00:02,262 --> 00:00:12,337
Chocolate originated in Mesoamerica, where Olmecs, Mayans, and Aztecs used cacao beans as currency and consumed chocolate as a bitter ceremonial drink.

3
00:00:12,337 --> 00:00:19,000
Spanish colonizers brought cacao to Europe in the 16th century, adding sugar to transform its flavor.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:25,137
The first solid chocolate bar was produced in 1847 by J.S. Fry and Sons in England.

5
00:00:25,137 --> 00:00:33,862
Milk chocolate was invented in 1875 by Swiss confectioner Daniel Peter, using condensed milk developed by his neighbor Henri Nestle.

6
00:00:33,862 --> 00:00:45,487
The global chocolate industry now exceeds 100 billion dollars annually, though many cacao farmers earn below subsistence wages and the industry confronts child labor and deforestation challenges.

